* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
# .sql is pinned for a reason beyond tidiness: a migration file's body must md5-match
# `schema_migrations.statements`, and that hash is over LF bytes. Without this line
# `* text=auto` plus core.autocrlf=true checks .sql out as CRLF on Windows, and the check
# that proves a recorded migration is the one that ran fails for every file at once.
*.sql text eol=lf
# and `applied.md5` is the other half of that same check — a record of those hashes.
*.md5 text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
# .json was the one text type left to `* text=auto`, so on Windows with core.autocrlf=true it
# checked out CRLF — and src/lab/social/__fixtures__/fourrow-wire.json is a recording that
# roomWire.test.ts compares BYTE FOR BYTE (imported ?raw). Measured 27 Nov 2026: 36 carriage
# returns on disk, 0 in the blob, and the pre-push suite failing on every Windows checkout
# while CI on Linux passed. A fixture is bytes, so it has to arrive as the bytes it was.
*.json text eol=lf